@format 1
@id section-naming.shortcut-popup
@title Rename selected section from shortcut popup
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry rename-dispatch
@summary Open the Viewfinder-centered SectionRename popup for the selected Split section, edit main name/prefix/suffix, and commit only on Enter; Escape, outside dismissal, or Flow close discard popup buffers.
@related section-naming.common.keyboard-shortcut, section-naming.common.apply-name-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag name
@tag rename
@tag shortcut
@tag popup

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias viewfinder = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PViewfinder

[rename-dispatch] nameSection accepted by Flow shortcut dispatcher <input>
- PFlowShortcutDispatch calls PFlowNameShow when section UI is active; the dispatcher does not require section editability @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / nameSection
> selection-check

[selection-check] Selected section exists <decision>
- PFlowNameShow reads the current section list and requires a valid LSegmentSelectionRead index @ flow.PFlowNameShow(...)
@ segment.LSegmentSelectionRead(...)
? "No valid selection" > not-opened
? "Selection valid" > close-old-popup

[not-opened] Shortcut not handled <output>
= PFlowNameShow returns false and no naming popup opens.

[close-old-popup] Close any previous naming popup <process>
- PFlowNameShow first closes an existing pFlowNamePopup before building a new one for the selected section, so another rename command replaces the prior popup @ flow.PFlowNameClose(...)
> build-fields

[build-fields] Build name, prefix, and suffix fields <process>
- Initialize all three TextBoxes from the selected LPiece; empty prefix/suffix boxes and separators start collapsed, while existing affixes start visible @ flow.PFlowNameShow(...)
@ flow.PFlowNameBuild(...)
@ flow.PFlowAffixShow(...)
> position-popup

[position-popup] Position popup over selected Viewfinder section <process>
- Read the selected section rectangle and create a centered Popup with StaysOpen=false; then open it, focus the main-name box, and select all name text @ viewfinder.PViewfinderSectionRead(...)
@ flow.PFlowNameShow(...)
> popup-input

[popup-input] Popup interaction <decision>
= Name, prefix, and suffix remain temporary TextBox state until an explicit Enter commit.
? "Ordinary text" > editing
? "Comma" > comma-step
? "Enter" > apply-fields
? "Escape" > cancel-explicit
? "Click/focus outside popup" > dismiss-outside
? "Flow closes" > flow-close

[editing] Continue editing popup fields <output>
= No LPiece name state changes yet.

[comma-step] Step to next affix field <output>
- PFlowStepAttach consumes comma input; when a next field exists it reveals/focuses/selects it, and comma in the suffix field is consumed without inserting text @ flow.PFlowStepAttach(...)

[cancel-explicit] Escape discards popup buffers <output>
- Escape calls PFlowNameClose without PFlowNameApply, so stored section name fields are unchanged @ flow.PFlowNameClose(...)

[dismiss-outside] Popup auto-dismisses without commit <output>
= StaysOpen is false; clicking/focusing outside auto-closes the Popup without calling PFlowNameApply.

[flow-close] Flow shutdown discards popup buffers <output>
- PFlowClose calls PFlowNameClose; pending popup text is not applied @ flow.PFlowClose(...)
@ flow.PFlowNameClose(...)

[apply-fields] Trim popup fields and request name change <process>
- Enter on any popup field calls PFlowNameApply, which trims main name/prefix/suffix and calls PFlowNameSet; the handler then closes the popup and marks Enter handled @ flow.PFlowNameApply(...)
@ flow.PFlowNameClose(...)
> map:section-naming.common.apply-name-state
